Let a profession tool banked in the reagent vault satisfy a recipe, in place.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp

Why: bug report #29 -- "Bought a blacksmith hammer, didn't go into inventory
or into reagent bank, need it for crafting."

Tools are reagent-vault material by IsReagentItem, so one is pulled out of
the bag the moment it is acquired. That half worked. What did not work is
that a banked tool cannot satisfy the recipe that needs it:

  Reagent[]        materials      TopUpReagentFromVault covers this
  Totem[]          a named item   nothing covered this
  TotemCategory[]  a tool kind    nothing covered this

Totem[] and TotemCategory[] are checked in CheckItems with HasItemCount /
HasItemTotemCategory, both of which walk real inventory only. So the hammer
was banked, visible in the reagent panel, and useless -- every blacksmithing
recipe still said you needed a hammer. Core-patch 0020 explicitly left totem
requirements alone; this is the follow-up, and it covers them by ANSWERING
the check rather than waiving it, which is the right shape for a requirement
that is real.

Nothing is moved. The first cut of this withdrew the tool into the player's
bags, which worked but quietly emptied the bank the player had deliberately
filed it into -- and the point of the reagent bank is that things stay there
and still count. A tool is not consumed, so there is nothing to supply: the
check only ever needed a truthful "yes, you have one".

The Gnomish Army Knife falls out for free. It is ITEM_CLASS_TRADE_GOODS / 3
rather than a weapon, so the old IsToolItem missed it, and its totem category
(161) has a mask that is a superset of the individual tools'. Because the
vault side asks the engine's own IsTotemCategoryCompatiableWith, one banked
Army Knife satisfies blacksmithing, engineering and the rest with no special
case anywhere.

Paired with two module-side changes in LivingGear_Vault.cpp:
  - IsToolItem also accepts trade goods carrying a totem category, so the
    Army Knife, enchanting rods, the Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor and the
    Jeweler's Kit are recognised as tools. It still does NOT reach
    ARMOR/relics or the shaman totem items, which are gear, not tools.
  - DefaultLootAction banks only the FIRST copy of a tool; later copies stay
    in the bag. The bot accounts had 30-75 Blacksmith Hammers apiece, which
    is a tool sink rather than a convenience.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ near the other Living Gear forward declarations
+bool LivingGear_VaultHasToolCategory(Player* player, uint32 totemCategory);
+bool LivingGear_VaultHasItem(Player* player, uint32 itemId);

@@ Spell::CheckItems, the Totem[] check
             if (m_spellInfo->Totem[i] != 0)
             {
-                if (player->HasItemCount(m_spellInfo->Totem[i]))
+                if (player->HasItemCount(m_spellInfo->Totem[i])
+                    || LivingGear_VaultHasItem(player, m_spellInfo->Totem[i]))
                 {
                     totems -= 1;
                     continue;
                 }
             }

@@ Spell::CheckItems, the TotemCategory[] check
             if (m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i] != 0)
             {
-                if (player->HasItemTotemCategory(m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i]))
+                if (player->HasItemTotemCategory(m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i])
+                    || LivingGear_VaultHasToolCategory(player, m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i]))
                 {
                     TotemCategory -= 1;
                     continue;
                 }
             }
